// REJECTS: baseUrl should not end with '/'
//
// A ServiceStoreConnection whose `baseUrl` ends in '/'. The whole grammar of this element is
// two fields, `store` and `baseUrl: STRING`, and both are present and syntactically perfect.
// The rejection comes from ServiceStoreConnectionParseTreeWalker:61 inspecting the LAST
// CHARACTER of a string literal.
//
// This is value validation at its purest -- a two-token grammar with a content rule on one of
// them -- and it is the most easily lost kind, because a trailing slash on a base url is
// harmless everywhere else in software. Combined with the service-side rule that a `path:`
// must START with '/' (see ./neg-servicestore-path-param-not-in-path.pure for that walker),
// legend-engine is enforcing a specific concatenation contract at parse time.
//
// ../fixtures/t2-servicestore.pure writes 'http://example.org' for exactly this reason.
###Connection
ServiceStoreConnection fixture::neg::TrailingSlashBaseUrl
{
  store: fixture::neg::Store;
  baseUrl: 'http://example.org/';
}
